title: A view follows the overrides of its root's author, unless it is switched to another author's perspective, the user's or a foreign owner's.
pid: 64a8d27d-4356-42ba-a6a6-93101b273597
body: |2-
  Built 2026-11-12 ('override_follower_of_tree_containing' in
  'server/dbs/in_rust_graph/override_resolution.rs'), at Jeff's request
  in [[id:cf937aed-c55e-4dd0-8916-729d226d0d04][Let's make following foreign overrides possible.]]: a view rooted
  at a foreign note shows what its author would see there. Under one's
  own root, a fork included, one's own overrides are followed, as
  before. Each top-level tree of a buffer decides for itself, so a
  search buffer or a multi-root view can mix the two. The save's
  overridesHere tamper check asks of the same author, so a carrier
  honest under one root is rejected under another.
  Since 2026-11-14 a view can be switched among perspectives: the root
  authors' (the default, as above), and each author's whose overrides
  would draw the buffer otherwise, followed in every tree, the roots
  included, so the buffer shows what that author would see (Emacs
  'C-c v o', Neovim '<localleader>vo', skg-for-ai 'override-perspective';
  the "set overrides followed" request: 'docs/api-and-formats.org').
  Jeff asked first for a switch to his own, on reading Tracy's notes
  from a view rooted at one of Top's, where his overrides did not show;
  then, the same day, that it cycle among every author, name each, and
  replace the root too. A switch redraws the buffer and is refused
  while it has unsaved edits. The decisions below were made by the two
  minds lent to Sue to build it, but where they say Jeff's.
contains:
- ff5001fe-8347-44a8-a6c1-e71c06acd044
- a4ad022b-258c-48c3-879d-f9c05ef61cb1
- eef0d82e-e427-467f-a38b-4d4b319ebe96
